spans.s:
प्र-शंस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be praised, com-
mendable, praiseworthy, laudable; preferable, better;
[cf. 1. प्र-शस्य.]

प्र-शास्त्र, अम्, n., Ved. the office of Praśāstṛ;
the Soma vessel of the Praśāstṛ; (Sāy.) = प्रशास्तुर्
यागः.

प्राशन, अम्, n. the act of eating, feeding upon,
tasting; causing to eat or taste [cf. अन्न-प्˚];
feeding (especially applied in Manu

प्र-सित, अस्, आ, अम्, bound to, bound, fastened;
adhering to or engaged in, diligent, attentive,
zealous; attached or devoted to, engrossed by;
(अम्), n. pus, matter.

प्र-सरत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, going forwards, proceed-
ing, projecting; spreading out, spreading, expanding;
bursting.

प्र-सृति, इस्, f. progress, advance; streaming,
flowing; the palm of the hand hollowed, a handful;
a measure equal to two Palas.

प्रस्तूत प्र-स्तूत, अस्, m., N. of a class of
deities under Manu Cākṣuṣa; (an incorrect form
for प्र-भूत or प्र-सूत.)

प्रस्तोभ प्र-स्तोभ, अस्, m. (fr. rt. स्तुभ्
with प्र), allusion to, reference to (with gen.);
रयेर् आङ्गिरसस्य प्रस्तोभः, N. of a Sāman.

प्र-स्फुट, अस्, आ, अम्, cleft open, expanded,
blown; manifest, clear, plain, apparent, evident;
divulged, published, spread abroad.

प्र-स्फोटन, अम्, n. splitting, falling asunder;
expanding, budding, opening, blooming; ripening;
causing to blow or bloom; making evident or mani-
fest, revealing; striking, beating; threshing or win-
nowing corn; a winnowing basket; wiping away,
rubbing out.

प्रास्त, अस्, आ, अम्, thrown away, thrown off;
thrown into, thrown, cast, hurled, discharged; ex-
pelled, turned out, banished.
